cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  tpsreg: a GUI for multimodal microscopy image registration using thin-plate
  splines
message: If you use this software in published work, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: James
    family-names: Lamb
    email: lambjames18@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/lambjames18/tps-image-registration-gui
abstract: >-
  A desktop application for aligning multimodal microscopy data using a
  thin-plate spline transformation fitted to matched control points. Supports
  2D images and 3D serial-sectioning stacks, EBSD formats (.ang, .h5,
  .dream3d) alongside standard image formats, and optional automatic control
  point detection with a pretrained deep-learning matcher.
keywords:
  - image registration
  - thin-plate spline
  - electron microscopy
  - EBSD
  - multimodal imaging
  - serial sectioning
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-03"
